# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# envs
.env.local.example
.env


# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...but the example file is documentation, not a secret. It must be
# committed or nobody knows which vars the app needs. Never put a real
# secret value in it — only blank keys and public identifiers.
!.env.local.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Internal working files — deliberately untracked (21 Aug 2026).
#
# These stay on disk and are still the source of truth locally; they are just
# not published to the public GitHub repo. Note they DO exist in commits up to
# and including eea96e5, which is already pushed — untracking stops future
# changes from being published, it does not remove the copies already in
# history. Removing those would need a history rewrite and a force push.
#
# AGENTS.md is regenerated by `next dev` on every run, so it is ignored rather
# than deleted; expect it to keep reappearing on disk.
/design-reference/
/AGENTS.md
/ARCHITECTURE.md
/BUILD_PLAN.md
/CLAUDE.md
